# No em dashes

Never use the em dash character (`-`, U+2014) or en dash (`-`, U+2013) anywhere in this project.

That includes:
- User-facing UI copy (titles, toasts, empty states, buttons, dialogs)
- Comments and docstrings
- README / markdown
- HTML titles and meta descriptions
- Scripts, workflows, and log messages
- CSS comments

Use a regular hyphen (`-`), a colon, a period, or rephrase the sentence instead.

Empty / missing-value placeholders should be `-` or `n/a`, never `-`.

If you see an existing em dash while editing, remove it in the same change.
